---
description: DevOps house conventions - apply when editing a container build, a compose topology, or a CI/CD workflow.
globs: "**/Dockerfile,**/Dockerfile.*,**/*.Dockerfile,**/docker-compose*.yml,**/docker-compose*.yaml,**/compose.yml,**/compose.yaml,**/.github/workflows/*.yml,**/.github/workflows/*.yaml"
alwaysApply: false
---

Editing a container build, a compose topology, or a CI/CD pipeline - load the `devops` skill under
`.cursor/skills/` before the edit; skip the load when it is already in context (the devops seats
preload it). Conventions are the source of truth, not recall. Covers Dockerfiles, compose files, and
GitHub Actions workflows - the delivery surface.

If the `devops` skill is not loaded, hold the line on the highest-value rules: pin a base image and
an action by digest or an exact tag rather than floating `:latest`, keep secrets out of the image and
the log (a build arg is not a secret store), and make the build reproducible - no unpinned
`apt-get install` of whatever is newest today.

Deploy scripts and the Aspire AppHost are the same concern but do not match these globs - load
`devops` yourself when editing them.

This is guidance, auto-attached by glob (not a hard block). Skip one-line tweaks.
